			"Message": "fix(Output): Route polyfill diagnostics through Mountain IPC and suppress errors\n\nIn `Disable/Lazy/Paint.ts`, removed direct `console.error` calls in polyfill callbacks. Replaced with silent error swallowing to prevent stack traces for non-fatal lifecycle errors.\n\nIn `Telemetry/Consent/Off.ts`, replaced direct `console.log` with a conditional `MountainIPCInvoke` call targeting `diagnostic:log`. This aligns the telemetry notification with the unified diagnostic pipeline established in recent commits, ensuring consent status appears in `Mountain.dev.log` rather than the browser console.\n\nBoth changes ensure that `Output` polyfill artifacts rely on the Rust backend for diagnostics and do not pollute the runtime console with expected behavior errors.",
			"SHA": "50dd492ca0b69e13a675a9931a7ee21fdd3ea6ed"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:53:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Route plugin polyfill diagnostics through Mountain IPC\n\nReplace direct `console.*` calls in Eager plugin polyfills (Activation, Idle/Value, Lifecycle/Phase) and the CEL Extension Scanner Service with a unified `_CELLog` helper. This helper invokes the `MountainIPCInvoke` command to forward diagnostic messages to the Rust backend's `diagnostic:log` handler.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Introduced `_CELLog` helper in polyfill files to safely bridge browser context logs to the Tauri/Mountain layer.\n- Updated `Source/Service/CEL/Extensions/Scanner/Service.ts` to forward warnings via `diagnostic:log` instead of stdout.\n- Ensures runtime logs from the `Output` bundled artifacts appear in `Mountain.dev.log` alongside native Rust events, aiding unified debugging.\n\nThis change eliminates reliance on browser developer tools for extension activation and scanner diagnostics within the Tauri runtime.",
			"SHA": "716eff424c76065b7d3a5446d16a8f8e11c7326e"
		},
